# Installation

## Prerequisites

- **SvelteKit** with Svelte 5
- **Tailwind CSS v4**
- **Node.js** >= 20

## Install the Package

```bash
# pnpm (recommended)
pnpm add fancy-ui-svelte

# npm
npm install fancy-ui-svelte

# bun
bun add fancy-ui-svelte
```

## Tailwind CSS Setup

FancyUI components use Tailwind CSS v4. Make sure your project has Tailwind configured. FancyUI ships a supplementary stylesheet you can import:

```css
/* In your app.css or layout.css */
@import "tailwindcss";
@import "fancy-ui-svelte/tailwind.css";
```

## Usage

Import any component directly:

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import { BorderBeam, Sparkles, RainbowButton } from 'fancy-ui-svelte';
</script>

<div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-xl border p-8">
  <RainbowButton>Click me</RainbowButton>
  <BorderBeam colorFrom="#9E7AFF" colorTo="#FE8BBB" />
</div>
```

## TypeScript

All components export their prop types:

```typescript
import { type BorderBeamProps } from 'fancy-ui-svelte';
```

## Peer Dependencies

FancyUI requires these as peer dependencies:

| Package | Version |
|---------|---------|
| `svelte` | `^5.0.0` |
| `tailwindcss` | `^4.0.0` |

Some components have additional runtime dependencies (`gsap`, `three`, `canvas-confetti`) which are bundled with the package.
